    card title "Two of 23 share a birthday?"

A: Twenty-three people in a room. What is the chance that two of them share a birthday?
    draw cake n23

B: Twenty-three out of three hundred and sixty-five days? That sounds tiny. Maybe six percent?
    draw chance guess6

    ask "In a room of 23 people, what is the chance that two share a birthday? Click on the line." on chance store p default "6"
        right: Close: you said {p}, and it is {p.true}.
        wrong: You said {p}. It is {p.true}: better than a coin flip.

    erase guess6

B: Half? With only twenty-three people? That can't be right.
    highlight chance

A: The trick is that it's not just your birthday against everyone else's. Every person is compared with every other person.
    draw crowd pairs

Twenty-three people make two hundred and fifty-three pairs, and each pair is a fresh chance of a match.
    group links members ["ln0_5","ln0_11","ln1_6","ln1_12","ln2_7","ln2_13","ln3_8","ln3_14","ln4_9","ln4_15","ln5_10","ln5_16","ln6_11","ln6_17","ln7_12","ln7_18","ln8_13","ln8_19","ln9_14","ln9_20","ln10_15","ln10_21","ln11_16","ln11_22","ln12_17","ln12_0","ln13_18","ln13_1","ln14_19","ln14_2","ln15_20","ln15_3","ln16_21","ln16_4","ln17_22","ln17_5","ln18_0","ln18_6","ln19_1","ln19_7","ln20_2","ln20_8","ln21_3","ln21_9","ln22_4","ln22_10"]
    parallel true

B: So it's not twenty-three tries. It's two hundred and fifty-three.
    highlight n23 effect underline

A: Right. Each pair matches only once in three hundred an (@draw each@)d sixty-five, but with that many tries, missing every single time gets unlikely.

    erase pairs each crowd links

B: And a bigger room? Say, seventy people?
    draw seventy

A: Then a shared birthday is all but certain: ninety-nine point nine percent.
    highlight seventy

B: Next office party, I'm taking bets.
    highlight seventy
